# Product work waits on staging for the on-device pass (CLAUDE.md, Doctrine 7).
# main is production: a push there deploys.
work=staging
promote=main
escape=PAL_PROMOTE

# Runs on EVERY commit including a promote, because it is about WHAT is being
# committed rather than where. Deliberately not in CI and not in `npm run check`:
# it compares this tree against `origin/main` as of the moment of the commit, and
# on a runner after a promote origin/main is already the merge — so a CI step
# would be red by construction for a window on every release. Hub LESSONS 128.
also=tools/branch-state-check.mjs
#
# And the hub commit is written in two files here — the marker this repo has
# reconciled with, and the pin CI checks the hub out at to run the shared
# gates. They are the same fact and they drift silently, and when they do the
# shared gates go green while running rules this repo has already adopted and
# they have never heard of. It is repo-local ON PURPOSE, because a gate
# validating the pin cannot itself be fetched at that pin. (Hub LESSONS §117.)
also=tools/hub-pin-check.mjs
#
# And a change to what the app SERVES has to carry a version, or the service
# worker stays byte-identical and no installed app ever fetches it. Four
# stylesheets had their dimmed-text colours corrected on staging with no bump:
# green on every gate, correct in the repo, and it would have reached nobody who
# already had the app. Same shape and same placement as branch-state-check — it
# compares the tree against origin/main at the moment of the commit, and after a
# promote the two are one commit, so it passes trivially.
also=tools/shipped-version-check.mjs
